    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n111084" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φῐλο-γέλως</span></b> , ὁ, ἡ, gen. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ωτος</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>laughter-loving,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Παρθένος Νίκη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Men.
					616
				</span></i>
			: acc. pl. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φιλογέλωτας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>R.</u>
					388e
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				1389b10
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐναντίον τὸ ὀδυρτικὸν τῷ
				φιλογέλωτι</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				1390a24
			</span></i>:— also acc. sg. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φιλόγελων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Jul.
					<u>Caes.</u>
					308d
				</span></i>
			 (but dat. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-γέλωτι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Mis.</u>
					346a
				</span></i>
			): gen. sg. neut. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φιλόγελω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Philostr.
					<u>VS</u>
					1
				</span></i>
			,<i><span class="en">
				21.5
			</span></i>; nom. pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φιλόγελω</span> (leg.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-γελῳ</span>) 
				Att.
			 for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φιλογέλωτες</span> acc. to
				Moer.<i><span class="en">
				p.385
			</span></i> P.: acc. pl. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φιλόγελως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Thphr.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					124
				</span></i>
			. </div>
